# Deploy policy

Ship only through `deploy.sh` at the repo root. Do not call `bai --build-push-image` or `bai --deploy-image` yourself. The script owns `-se`, the per-unit loop, the RTDB config walk, the `env/<env>` tag, and the restore to `-se=local`.

Local Docker is not required. Cloud Build builds the image. `gcloud` must be authenticated. `deploy.sh` puts the Cloud SDK on `PATH` and falls back to application-default credentials. Do not export `PATH` or run `gcloud config set` from the chat.

## Version

`version-app.json` at the repo root is the app version (`{"version":"x.y.z"}`). Bump patch unless the user asked for minor or major. Tag `v<version>` and push the tag. Do not add a second `VERSION` file. Do not force-move `v*` tags.

`env/<env>` is a moving pointer. `deploy.sh` force-moves it after a successful deploy. That is the only force-tag this repo allows.

## Sequence

1. Clean tree, branch pushed, no divergence.
2. If any `__package.json` changed in the commits being shipped: `bash build-and-install.sh -i -nb`. Otherwise `bash build-and-install.sh -nb` is enough when deps did not change. Never `bai -i -up=<subset>`.
3. Build and `bai -t -up=@app` pass.
4. Commit the version bump, tag `v<version>`, push commit and tag.
5. `bash deploy.sh build <version> staging` then `bash deploy.sh deploy <version> staging`.
6. Smoke-check staging. If it is unhealthy, `bash deploy.sh deploy <previous> staging` and stop.
7. Prod only after an explicit user yes: `DEPLOY_CONFIRM_PROD=yes bash deploy.sh deploy <version> prod`. Same artifact. Do not rebuild between staging and prod.

`env` defaults to `staging`. The script refuses `local` and refuses `prod` without `DEPLOY_CONFIRM_PROD=yes`.

## Config deltas

Module config that must land in RTDB goes in `releases/<semver>.json` (`default` and/or `app` only). See `releases/README.md`. The deploy script applies the walk after the backend revision is serving. Do not PATCH `/_config` yourself.

## Fill before the first real deploy

`containerDeployment` / `hostingDeployment` artifact project and region in the app `__package.json` files (mirrored by `bai-config.json` `ARTIFACT_PROJECT_ID` and `ARTIFACT_REGION`), plus `imageName` and `packageName`, and the `replace-dev` / `replace-staging` / `replace-prod` project ids. Until those are real, deploy will fail closed.

The staging deploy **service account lives in GCP**. Create it with `bash scripts/create-staging-deploy-sa.sh <slug> <staging-project-id>`. The JSON key is written to `$HOME/.config/gcloud/<slug>-staging-deploy.json` only. Never commit it. `gcloud builds submit` needs `roles/storage.admin` on `gs://nu-art-dev-ops_cloudbuild` and `roles/serviceusage.serviceUsageConsumer` on `nu-art-dev-ops`.
